  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "If you discard Loxodon Smiter and put it onto the battlefield, you've still discarded a card. Abilities that trigger when you discard a card (such as the one from Liliana's Caress) will still trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "18ac2282-83af-4acc-b20b-6a95771da688",
      "published_at": "2012-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This has basic land types, but it isn't a basic land. Things that affect basic lands don't affect it. Things that affect basic land types do.",
      "oracle_id": "703243f0-8cb3-420f-958f-5fd4bde30293",
      "published_at": "2008-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This has the mana abilities associated with both of its basic land types.",
      "oracle_id": "703243f0-8cb3-420f-958f-5fd4bde30293",
      "published_at": "2008-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A creature is \"enchanted\" if it has any Auras attached to it.",
      "oracle_id": "a6fd90dc-0ec3-4dce-a77a-4d04f5e254bf",
      "published_at": "2005-08-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If there are fewer than twenty cards in the targeted player's library, that player puts all the cards from their library into their graveyard.",
      "oracle_id": "cc2b6e58-2d6f-495e-95f3-9496105c4cba",
      "published_at": "2009-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A split card's characteristics are a combination of its two halves while it is not on the stack. For example, Assault // Battery has a mana value of 5 while it is in your library. If an effect allows you to search your library for a card with mana value 4 or less, you can't find Assault // Battery.",
      "oracle_id": "e119ba58-85e4-49ec-a2f8-3d094187c99d",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each split card has two names. If an effect instructs you to choose a card name, you may choose one of those names, but not both.",
      "oracle_id": "e119ba58-85e4-49ec-a2f8-3d094187c99d",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each split card is a single card. For example, if you discard a split card, you've discarded one card, not two. If an effect counts the number of sorcery cards in your graveyard, Assault // Battery counts once, not twice.",
      "oracle_id": "e119ba58-85e4-49ec-a2f8-3d094187c99d",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect allows you to cast a spell with certain characteristics, consider only the characteristics of the half you're casting. For example, if an effect allows you to cast a sorcery spell with mana value 2 or less from among cards in your graveyard, you could cast Assault this way, but not Battery.",
      "oracle_id": "e119ba58-85e4-49ec-a2f8-3d094187c99d",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you copy a spell that's half of a split card, the copy copies that same half. For example, if you copy Assault, the copy is also Assault, not Battery.",
      "oracle_id": "e119ba58-85e4-49ec-a2f8-3d094187c99d",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Split cards have two card faces on a single card. The characteristics of the half you didn't cast are ignored while the spell is on the stack.",
      "oracle_id": "e119ba58-85e4-49ec-a2f8-3d094187c99d",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To cast a split card, choose one of its halves to cast. There's no way to cast both halves of this split card.",
      "oracle_id": "e119ba58-85e4-49ec-a2f8-3d094187c99d",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
